297Z"}, "id": 9, "domain": "VFD / Variable Frequency Drive Faults & Operation", "difficulty": "medium", "type": "calculation", "correct_answer": "B", "model_answer": "C", "parse_rule": "leading_letter", "is_correct": false, "http": 200, "turn_status": "answered", "basis": "general_reasoning", "trace_id": "a4d82e4c7607fd0ce3ff9e629e53a617", "response_time_ms": 5221, "answer_text": "C\n\nRunning at 30 Hz cuts the shaft speed to about half of the 60 Hz speed. Fan power varies roughly with the cube of speed, so power ≈(½)³ ≈ 0.125 of full‑speed power – about one‑eighth (12.5%)."}
