"id": 24, "domain": "Motor Theory & Troubleshooting", "difficulty": "hard", "type": "scenario", "correct_answer": "D", "model_answer": "C", "parse_rule": "leading_letter", "is_correct": false, "http": 200, "turn_status": "answered", "basis": "general_reasoning", "trace_id": "3392416487716bd2a0cc7028cce057d6", "response_time_ms": 5325, "answer_text": "C\n\n- The two equal low readings (T1‑T2 and T2‑T3) and the third reading exactly double them (T1‑T3) are what you expect for a balanced three‑phase motor measured phase‑to‑phase.  \n- Verify the motor is indeed wired in delta (or that the test leads are connected phase‑to‑phase, not phase‑to‑neutral).  \n- If you suspect a wiring error, de‑energize, lock‑out/tag‑out, and confirm the motor’s connection diagram matches the measured configuration.  \n\n(I'm answering from general knowledge; check the motor’s own manual to confirm the expected resistance values.)"}
