, "domain": "Industrial Sensors, Instrumentation & Signals", "difficulty": "hard", "type": "recall", "correct_answer": "A", "model_answer": "A", "parse_rule": "leading_letter", "is_correct": true, "http": 200, "turn_status": "answered", "basis": "general_reasoning", "trace_id": "2bd96799a9344362b41d4c6d648cf2f3", "response_time_ms": 5193, "answer_text": "A\n\nThe primary difference is that a PT1000 has a base resistance of 1 kΩ at 0 °C versus 100 Ω for a PT100, which makes the PT1000 far less sensitive to errors introduced by the resistance of the lead wires."}
